      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(process): add gemini and claude to Windows .cmd shim allowlist",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n- On Windows, using the `google-gemini-cli` provider fails with `spawn gemini ENOENT` because Node's `child_process.spawn` does not automatically resolve `.cmd` extensions (only `.exe`/`.com`)\n- npm global installs on Windows create `.cmd` shim files, so `gemini` (and `claude`) need the `.cmd` suffix to be found by `spawn`\n- Fixes #98573\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe supervisor child adapter (`src/process/supervisor/adapters/child.ts`) has a `resolveCommand` function that uses `resolveWindowsCommandShim` with a hardcoded allowlist of commands that should get `.cmd` appended on Windows. The list included `npm`, `pnpm`, `yarn`, and `npx` but not `gemini` or `claude` — so spawning those CLI tools failed on Windows.\n\n## What Was Changed\n\n- Added `gemini` and `claude` to the `cmdCommands` allowlist in `src/process/supervisor/adapters/child.ts:26`\n- This triggers the same `.cmd` resolution + `cmd.exe` wrapping mechanism already used and verified for `pnpm`, `yarn`, `npm`, and `npx`\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR is intentionally narrow: **allowlist-only**. The shared `cmd.exe` metacharacter escaping change has been split out to a follow-up PR to keep the shell-boundary review separate from the shim resolution fix.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Windows users can now use the `google-gemini-cli` and `claude-cli` providers without encountering `ENOENT` spawn errors\n- No change on macOS or Linux (platform guard already skips non-Windows)\n- No change to the shared `cmd.exe` escaping path (metacharacter rejection behavior is unchanged)\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real Windows Machine (MINGW64, Node.js v22.19.0)\n\n**Bug:** `spawn(\"gemini\") -> ENOENT`, `spawn(\"gemini.cmd\") -> EINVAL` (CVE-2024-27980)  \n**Fix:** `cmd.exe /d /s /c \"gemini.cmd --version\" -> exit 0`\n\n### npm package evidence\n`@google/gemini-cli` declares `{\"gemini\":\"bundle/gemini.js\"}` -> Windows npm creates `gemini.cmd`\n\n### CI evidence\n- `checks-windows-node-test` on `windows-latest`: all process tests pass on real Windows\n- All unit tests pass via `setPlatform(\"win32\")` simulation\n\n## Tests\n\n```bash\npnpm test src/process/supervisor/adapters/child.test.ts  # 21 tests, 20 pass (1 pre-existing Linux failure)\npnpm test src/process/windows-command.test.ts  # 4 tests pass\n```\n\nNew tests added:\n- `wraps gemini CLI command through trusted cmd.exe on Windows (#98573)` — verifies `gemini` -> `gemini.cmd` wrapped via `cmd.exe`\n- `wraps claude CLI command through trusted cmd.exe on Windows` — same for `claude`\n- `keeps gemini command unchanged on non-Windows platforms (#98573)` — verifies no `.cmd` suffix on Linux\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] No: Does this change affect user-visible behavior? (Only affects Windows CLI tool spawning, restoring expected behavior)\n- [x] No: Does this change affect configuration surface?\n- [x] No: Does this change affect security? (No change to security model; same allowlist pattern used for other CLI tools like pnpm/npm/yarn)\n- [x] No: Does this change affect plugin APIs?\n- [x] No: Does this change require documentation updates?",
        "branch": "fix/gemini-cli-windows-cmd-shim",
